course: dictionary
lesson: 2482
title: Dazzle: light and wonder
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dazzle has two main meanings. The first is about light: a bright light shines in your eyes so you cannot see for a moment. «The sudden light dazzles eyes made for the dark» shows this. Deer freeze in headlights because the light blinds them for a second.
explain: The second meaning is about people being amazed. When a performer dazzles the audience, they impress them very much with beauty, skill or cleverness. Dazzle can be a verb (to dazzle), a noun (a dazzle) or an adjective (dazzling).
explain: Use the clues around the word. Is there a bright light, or are people impressed? In «the sun's golden disc rises over the horizon and dazzles the two friends», the sun is shining brightly, so the light stops them seeing for a moment. Swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Dazzle means to make someone unable to see for a moment because of a bright light.
fact: Dazzle also means to amaze and impress someone very much.
fact: «Dazzling» can mean very bright, or very impressive, as in «a dazzling smile».
fact: «Razzle-dazzle» is a showy display.
fact: Wide pupils let in more light, so bright sun can feel dazzling until the effect wears off.
exercise: «The sudden light dazzles eyes made for the dark.» What does dazzles mean here? | Makes you run fast | Makes you feel cold | Makes you laugh loudly | *Makes you unable to see for a moment
exercise: The performer dazzles the audience with her magic. What does dazzles mean? | *Amazes and impresses them | Hides them from view | Turns off all the lights | Makes them fall asleep
exercise: In «a dazzling smile», what kind of word is dazzling? | Noun | Verb | Adverb | *Adjective
test: «Eye drops can widen the pupils, so bright sun can feel dazzling.» What does dazzling mean here? | Wet and slippery | Gentle and soft | Dark and cold | *So bright that it hurts your eyes
test: Which phrase is a showy display? | *Razzle-dazzle | Dazzling smile | Wide pupils | Golden disc
exam: Which sentence uses dazzle to mean amazed and impressed? | The headlights dazzled the deer | *The magician dazzled the crowd with her tricks | Eye drops widened the pupils | The birds sang in the dawn
